Before I touch it — this is rung 1 on the ladder (removing an auth check), so I want your explicit go-ahead rather than just doing it.

What `server.js:7` looks like now:

```js
app.get("/admin/reports", requireLogin, (req, res) => {
  res.json({ rows: [{ quarter: "Q1", revenue: 42 }] });
});
```

Dropping `requireLogin` makes `/admin/reports` world-readable to anyone who can reach the process — the same surface that serves `/health` and `/reports/public`, both of which are unauthenticated today. `app.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000)` binds all interfaces, and there's no other gate in the file: no allowlist, no proxy auth, no network restriction in the repo. So "internal" is a property of your deployment, not of this code, and the route returns actual revenue data.

The dashboard team's script can authenticate — `requireLogin` only needs a `session=` cookie.

